{"id":1825181,"retrievedAt":"2026-11-14T17:07:13.776Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":null,"belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[],"homepage":"","id":1825181,"imdb_id":null,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_title":"Gilbert White Lived Here","overview":"A short documentary presented by David Attenborough on Gilbert White (1720–1793), the pioneering English naturalist, writer, and clergyman whose 1789 book The Natural History of Selborne has remained in print for more than two centuries.  Living almost his entire life in the Hampshire village of Selborne, White closely observed the plants, animals, and seasonal rhythms of his surroundings. He was the first to distinguish the harvest mouse, noctule bat, and chiffchaff as separate species, and his writings anticipated modern ecological thinking by showing how everything in nature—from earthworms to birds to human beings—is interconnected. Written with clarity, wit, and a lyrical style, the book has inspired generations of naturalists (including Attenborough), writers, and artists, and has made Selborne known to readers around the world.","popularity":0.0194,"poster_path":null,"production_companies":[{"id":3324,"logo_path":"/dqT3yOTlfJRmtvk52Ccd1O6dZ0A.png","name":"BBC","origin_country":"GB"}],"production_countries":[],"release_date":"1975-01-01","revenue":0,"runtime":15,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[{"english_name":"English","iso_639_1":"en","name":"English"}],"status":"Released","tagline":"","title":"Gilbert White Lived Here","video":false,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"credits":{"cast":[],"crew":[{"adult":false,"gender":2,"id":86543,"known_for_department":"Acting","name":"David Attenborough","original_name":"David Attenborough","popularity":1.6283,"profile_path":"/xE6aLZ2Ma1VSoZGhOUW8TcbBMN6.jpg","credit_id":"6af76ea35537ecb58c640861","department":"Crew","job":"Presenter"},{"adult":false,"gender":0,"id":1066806,"known_for_depar